---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import SectionIntro from '../components/SectionIntro.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import FaqItem from '../components/FaqItem.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ | She Who Remembers"
  description="Answers about where to begin, courses, private guidance, the book, and the limits of this work: coaching and education, not therapy or crisis care."
>
  <Hero
    heading="Questions"
    lede="Direct answers. No performance of mystery."
    surface="light"
    spacing="compact"
  >
    <p>
      If you are looking for a doorway rather than a definition, start at{' '}
      <TextLink href={withBase('/begin-here')}>Begin Here</TextLink>.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Starting">
        <p>You do not have to arrive already sorted.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <FaqList>
        <FaqItem question="Where should I begin?">
          <p>
            If you want to locate the season you are in, start at{' '}
            <TextLink href={withBase('/begin-here')}>Begin Here</TextLink>. If you already know
            you want a human conversation,{' '}
            <TextLink href={withBase('/book-a-conversation')}>Book a Conversation</TextLink>.
            The map of the work lives on{' '}
            <TextLink href={withBase('/the-work')}>The Work</TextLink>.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Do I need to read the book first?">
          <p>
            No. The book can deepen the language. It is not an entrance exam, and participation
            in a course or conversation does not depend on assigned reading.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Do I need to know which course I want?">
          <p>
            No. The name of the work can come later. If more than one doorway sounds familiar,
            choose the sentence that feels most true today. Comparison lives on{' '}
            <TextLink href={withBase('/courses')}>Courses & Experiences</TextLink>.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Do I need to identify as spiritual?">
          <p>
            No. Spiritual language may appear. Belief is not required. Curiosity, discernment,
            and a willingness to examine your own experience are enough.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
      </FaqList>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Courses">
        <p>Three pathways. Not a ladder.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <FaqList>
        <FaqItem question="How are the three pathways different?">
          <p>
            The Sacred No is voice and boundaries. The Remembering is self and embodiment. Legacy
            in Motion is purpose and transmission. Fuller descriptions are on{' '}
            <TextLink href={withBase('/courses')}>Courses & Experiences</TextLink>.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Do I need to take them in order?">
          <p>
            No. They are doors, not levels. Enter where the pressure in your life actually is.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Are current dates and prices available?">
          <p>
            Not on this website yet. Dates, duration, and fees will be named when an offering is
            actually open. Until then, a fit conversation is the honest next step rather than a
            guessed calendar.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="What if more than one pathway fits?">
          <p>
            That is ordinary. Start with the one that matches this season. The others can remain
            available without becoming homework.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
      </FaqList>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Private guidance">
        <p>Individualized work when a threshold needs more room.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <FaqList>
        <FaqItem question="What is private guidance?">
          <p>
            One-to-one support for a specific season, decision, boundary, or integration. It does
            not replace inner authority. Its purpose is to make your own discernment more
            available. See{' '}
            <TextLink href={withBase('/private-guidance')}>Private Guidance</TextLink>.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Do I need to be in crisis?">
          <p>
            No. Crisis needs care built for crisis. Private guidance is for a season that wants
            more room, not for emergency or acute mental health need.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Will Lala tell me what to do?">
          <p>
            No. You may be asked harder questions than you arrived with. The decisions remain
            yours.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Can I work with Lala while in therapy?">
          <p>
            The two may coexist when their roles stay clear. Therapy addresses what belongs in
            clinical care. This is coaching and educational work. It does not replace treatment.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="How do I know if private work is right for me?">
          <p>
            If the threshold is specific and needs more room than a group container, private work
            may fit. A{' '}
            <TextLink href={withBase('/book-a-conversation')}>fit conversation</TextLink> is
            where that gets sorted without requiring you to already know.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
      </FaqList>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Scope and safety">
        <p>What this work can hold, and what it must not pretend to hold.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <FaqList>
        <FaqItem question="Is this therapy?">
          <p>
            No. She Who Remembers is coaching and educational work: awareness, embodiment,
            boundaries, self-trust, and choice. It is not psychotherapy, diagnosis, or a
            substitute for mental health treatment.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Is this medical or psychiatric care?">
          <p>
            No. It is not medical advice, psychiatric care, or medication guidance. If those are
            needed, they remain needed.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Can this support relationship questions?">
          <p>
            Yes: your patterns, communication, and limits. It is not couples therapy, and it will
            not instruct you to stay or leave. Those choices, if they come, belong to you.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="What if I am in an unsafe situation?">
          <p>
            This website, the contact form, and a fit conversation are not crisis services. If
            you are in immediate danger, contact local emergency services or a trusted local
            resource. Do not use these pages as a substitute for urgent help.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Will I have to disclose trauma?">
          <p>
            No. There is no requirement to disclose traumatic experience or prove vulnerability.
            Material that requires trauma treatment belongs with an appropriately qualified
            professional.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Will I have to discuss sex or intimacy?">
          <p>
            No. Embodiment and body sovereignty may be discussed conceptually. Personal sexual
            disclosure is never required.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
      </FaqList>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="The book">
        <p>The source body of ideas. Not a product page with invented availability.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <FaqList>
        <FaqItem question="Is She Who Remembers required reading?">
          <p>
            No. The book can stand alone, and the rest of the work can be entered without it.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Where can I buy the book?">
          <p>
            A purchase link is not listed on this site yet. When a way to obtain the book is
            ready, it will be named on{' '}
            <TextLink href={withBase('/book')}>the book page</TextLink>.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Is the book available yet?">
          <p>
            Publication details are not listed here. This site will not invent a release date,
            retailer, or ISBN. When those facts are ready, they will appear plainly.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
      </FaqList>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If the question is still which door"
    primary={{ label: 'Begin Here', href: withBase('/begin-here') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Book a Conversation', href: withBase('/book-a-conversation') }}
  >
    <p>You do not have to collect every answer before you start.</p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>
